s-abdulel-sayed-clean-1.png 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2F16%2F696df430457cbaa5854ae5737f38%2Fnewsmakers-abdulel-sayed-clean-1.png 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2F16%2F696df430457cbaa5854ae5737f38%2Fnewsmakers-abdulel-sayed-clean-1.png 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2F16%2F696df430457cbaa5854ae5737f38%2Fnewsmakers-abdulel-sayed-clean-1.png 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2F16%2F696df430457cbaa5854ae5737f38%2Fnewsmakers-abdulel-sayed-clean-1.png 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2F16%2F696df430457cbaa5854ae5737f38%2Fnewsmakers-abdulel-sayed-clean-1.png 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2F16%2F696df430457cbaa5854ae5737f38%2Fnewsmakers-abdulel-sayed-clean-1.png" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2F16%2F696df430457cbaa5854ae5737f38%2Fnewsmakers-abdulel-sayed-clean-1.png" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F40%2F16%2F696df430457cbaa5854ae5737f38%2Fnewsmakers-abdulel-sayed-clean-1.png" class="img" alt="Abdul El-Sayed sits down for an NPR Newsmakers interview. He wears a black suit jacket and a black V-neck shirt underneath. His hands are in the air as he talks. " loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Abdul El-Sayed sits down for an NPR &lt;em&gt;Newsmakers&lt;/em&gt; interview.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Bronson Arcuri/NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Go face-to-face with the person of the moment. NPR's &lt;/em&gt;Newsmakers&lt;em&gt; video podcast brings the biggest names in politics, business, sports, arts, and culture out of the headlines and into the interview chair to discuss the mark they're making on the world. Follow the &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/podcasts/g-s1-114952/nprs-newsmakers" target="_blank"&gt;Newsmakers&lt;em&gt; podcast&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; or subscribe to &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.youtube.com/npr" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;NPR's YouTube channel&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; to get new episodes as soon as they're available.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Abdul El-Sayed has made history as the first Muslim elected to the U.S. Senate. The 42-year-old progressive from Michigan is already calling for a new direction for his party and urging President Trump to collaborate on actionable solutions. El-Sayed said that voters have temporarily entrusted Democrats with power, but warns that they risk losing that trust if they don't act boldly. As the senator-elect comes into the new role, he is advocating for new Democratic leadership in Congress, an end to the war in Iran, the passage of "Medicare for All" and the abolishment of ICE. While he acknowledges the challenge Senate Democrats face with a majority that's a few seats shy of being filibuster-proof, he remains open to working with his new Republican colleagues. In conversation with &lt;em&gt;Morning Edition&lt;/em&gt;'s Leila Fadel, El-Sayed reflects on the recent elections, the future of the Democratic Party and the need for impactful legislation in the upcoming years.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://lnk.to/gKEFX3NW" target="_blank"&gt;Watch or listen&lt;/a&gt; to the interview or &lt;a href="http://npr.org/2026/11/12/nx-s1-6034592/abdul-el-sayed-democratic-voters-mandate-trump-meeting" target="_blank"&gt;read the article&lt;/a&gt; about their discussion.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Deep dive&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-152726" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 8254;         --source-height: 4643;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8254x4643+0+430/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fcb%2Ffd%2Fa9c5ffc14790a6c95afded77f4f2%2Fgettyimages-2284066705.jpg" class="img" alt="Rows of vehicles lead up to an auto dealership with a Ford sign on it. " loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Ford Motor vehicles are displayed for sale at the Leif Johnson Ford dealership on June 30 in Austin, Texas.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Brandon Bell/Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;The average price for a new vehicle in the U.S. has hit a record high of $51,109, according to Kelley Blue Book. This figure is about $500 above the previous record set in December 2025. For years, car prices have remained high, primarily due to supply chain issues stemming from the pandemic. But there's some good news: While that new high sets a record, it only represents a 2.1% increase over the past year. This means the price is rising more slowly. If you're in the market for a car, &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/10/nx-s1-6026659/average-vehicle-price-record-high" target="_blank"&gt;here's what to know&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🚗 Used cars are also more expensive. The average used car now costs close to $27,00, 6% higher than last year, according to Cox Automotive.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🚗 New vehicles cost more partly because it takes more money for automakers to make them. Tariffs on steel, aluminum and imported goods from Canada affect American automakers, who assemble the vehicles on both sides of the border. Computer chips used in sensors and electronics also cost more, thanks to competing demand from data centers.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🚗 Americans tend to prefer larger vehicles, such as SUVs and trucks, which often come with a higher price tag, according to Kelley Blue Book.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🚗 Drivers today tend not to want entry-level cars. Instead, they are increasingly drawn to more expensive features, like 360-degree cameras, heated seats and parking assist systems.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-153049" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 3453;         --source-height: 1942;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3453x1942+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Feb%2F84%2Fa7cafb3943fc86f9e6e7ee072edc%2Fgettyimages-958767980.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3453x1942+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Feb%2F84%2Fa7cafb3943fc86f9e6e7ee072edc%2Fgettyimages-958767980.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3453x1942+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Feb%2F84%2Fa7cafb3943fc86f9e6e7ee072edc%2Fgettyimages-958767980.jpg 800w, https://npr