80.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3453x1942+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Feb%2F84%2Fa7cafb3943fc86f9e6e7ee072edc%2Fgettyimages-958767980.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3453x1942+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Feb%2F84%2Fa7cafb3943fc86f9e6e7ee072edc%2Fgettyimages-958767980.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3453x1942+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Feb%2F84%2Fa7cafb3943fc86f9e6e7ee072edc%2Fgettyimages-958767980.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3453x1942+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Feb%2F84%2Fa7cafb3943fc86f9e6e7ee072edc%2Fgettyimages-958767980.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3453x1942+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Feb%2F84%2Fa7cafb3943fc86f9e6e7ee072edc%2Fgettyimages-958767980.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3453x1942+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Feb%2F84%2Fa7cafb3943fc86f9e6e7ee072edc%2Fgettyimages-958767980.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3453x1942+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Feb%2F84%2Fa7cafb3943fc86f9e6e7ee072edc%2Fgettyimages-958767980.jpg" class="img" alt="U.S. actor Stacy Keach poses on May 15, 2018, during a photocall for the film &amp;quot;Gotti&amp;quot; at the 71st edition of the Cannes Film Festival in Cannes, southern France." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 U.S. actor Stacy Keach poses on May 15, 2018, during a photocall for the film "Gotti" at the 71st edition of the Cannes Film Festival in Cannes, southern France.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Anne-Christine Poujoulat/AFP via Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Actor Stacy Keach has &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/11/728054385/stacy-keach-dead" target="_blank"&gt;died at the age of 85&lt;/a&gt; after a long battle with a serious heart condition and heart failure. His diverse roles included policemen, cowboys and Shakespearean characters.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In this week's Far-Flung Postcards, NPR's Ricci Shryock sends greetings from Senegal, where breakdancers practice for their country's &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/11/g-s1-150228/senegal-youth-olympic-games-breakdancing" target="_blank"&gt;historic hosting of the Youth Olympic Games&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Russia's top independent newspaper, &lt;em&gt;Novaya Gazeta&lt;/em&gt;, is &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/10/nx-s1-6034460/russias-most-famous-independent-newspaper-has-shut-down-after-more-than-30-years" target="_blank"&gt;shutting down after more than 30 years&lt;/a&gt; due to Kremlin pressure from the Ukraine war and censorship laws.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
