lity/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F8c%2F6f%2Fdf477a534124b0b815fc6bce91db%2Fpromo-square-static.png 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1652x929+0+110/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F8c%2F6f%2Fdf477a534124b0b815fc6bce91db%2Fpromo-square-static.png 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1652x929+0+110/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F8c%2F6f%2Fdf477a534124b0b815fc6bce91db%2Fpromo-square-static.png 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1652x929+0+110/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F8c%2F6f%2Fdf477a534124b0b815fc6bce91db%2Fpromo-square-static.png 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1652x929+0+110/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F8c%2F6f%2Fdf477a534124b0b815fc6bce91db%2Fpromo-square-static.png 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1652x929+0+110/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F8c%2F6f%2Fdf477a534124b0b815fc6bce91db%2Fpromo-square-static.png 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1652x929+0+110/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F8c%2F6f%2Fdf477a534124b0b815fc6bce91db%2Fpromo-square-static.png 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1652x929+0+110/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F8c%2F6f%2Fdf477a534124b0b815fc6bce91db%2Fpromo-square-static.png" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1652x929+0+110/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F8c%2F6f%2Fdf477a534124b0b815fc6bce91db%2Fpromo-square-static.png" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1652x929+0+110/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F8c%2F6f%2Fdf477a534124b0b815fc6bce91db%2Fpromo-square-static.png" class="img" alt="A slowly animated composite of four illustrations shows shifting colors in the Arctic, in a blue lake, in an insect, and in a coral reef" loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Climate change is transforming the vibrant colors of nature, from Arctic landscapes to coral reefs. The effects of these color shifts are complex, and scientists are racing to understand them. Here's how climate change is &lt;a href="https://apps.npr.org/color-climate-change-coral-lakes/" target="_blank"&gt;altering the colors of the world&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;➡️ Every summer, climate-driven wildfires blanket Arctic ice in soot. These dark particles from oil and gas operations, commercial shipping and tourism absorb heat from the sun, accelerating melting ice and contributing to sea-level rise.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;➡️ As permafrost thaws deeper into the soil, nutrients become more available, enabling larger vegetation to take hold and turning the landscape greener. A 2020 study in &lt;em&gt;Nature Communications &lt;/em&gt;found that about 38% of sites in Alaska, Canada and western Eurasia showed greening.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;➡️ Thawing permafrost can also mix soil with lake water, turning them darker. A 2021 study in &lt;em&gt;Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America (PNAS)&lt;/em&gt; found green wavelengths in lakes in the boreal Arctic zone declined by 15% from 1984 to 2019, making these lakes appear darker to the naked eye. The darker a lake gets, the more heat it can store.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;➡️ Some insects have changed color due to warmer climates. North American male dragonflies are losing wing color, according to a study in &lt;em&gt;PNAS&lt;/em&gt;. This helps them stay cooler but also reduces the coloration that attracts females.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Picture show&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-152486" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 4000;         --source-height: 2250;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2250+0+374/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F27%2F4d4fe4984450a672595971ed542a%2Fdesert-bloom-t-merino-87.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2250+0+374/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F27%2F4d4fe4984450a672595971ed542a%2Fdesert-bloom-t-merino-87.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2250+0+374/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F27%2F4d4fe4984450a672595971ed542a%2Fdesert-bloom-t-merino-87.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2250+0+374/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F27%2F4d4fe4984450a672595971ed542a%2Fdesert-bloom-t-merino-87.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2250+0+374/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F27%2F4d4fe4984450a672595971e