-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F27%2F4d4fe4984450a672595971ed542a%2Fdesert-bloom-t-merino-87.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2250+0+374/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F27%2F4d4fe4984450a672595971ed542a%2Fdesert-bloom-t-merino-87.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2250+0+374/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F27%2F4d4fe4984450a672595971ed542a%2Fdesert-bloom-t-merino-87.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2250+0+374/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F27%2F4d4fe4984450a672595971ed542a%2Fdesert-bloom-t-merino-87.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2250+0+374/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F27%2F4d4fe4984450a672595971ed542a%2Fdesert-bloom-t-merino-87.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4000x2250+0+374/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F44%2F27%2F4d4fe4984450a672595971ed542a%2Fdesert-bloom-t-merino-87.jpg" class="img" alt="A field of colorful wildflowers blankets the Atacama Desert in northern Chile, transforming the world&amp;#039;s driest non-polar desert into a vibrant landscape during the rare flowering desert phenomenon, known locally as the Desierto Florido. This extraordinary event occurs when unusually heavy rainfall awakens seeds that have remained dormant beneath the desert soil for years, sometimes decades. Within weeks, thousands of flowers emerge, covering vast stretches of the desert in shades of pink, purple, yellow, and white. The blooms last only a few weeks before the flowers dry out and release their seeds, which remain in the soil until the next rainfall brings the desert back to life. Huasco, Chile, on Wednesday October 21, 2026. Tamara Merino for NPR." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 A field of colorful wildflowers blankets the Atacama Desert in northern Chile, transforming the world's driest non-polar desert into a vibrant landscape during the rare flowering desert phenomenon, known locally as the Desierto Florido. This extraordinary event occurs when unusually heavy rainfall awakens seeds that have remained dormant beneath the desert soil for years, sometimes decades. Within weeks, thousands of flowers emerge, covering vast stretches of the desert in shades of pink, purple, yellow, and white. The blooms last only a few weeks before the flowers dry out and release their seeds, which remain in the soil until the next rainfall brings the desert back to life. Huasco, Chile, on Wednesday October 21, 2026. Tamara Merino for NPR.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Tamera Merino for NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;The Atacama Desert in Chile has transformed into a vibrant patchwork of pinks, yellows, lilacs and purples, thanks to the El Niño super cycle. This floral bloom has been the largest and most colorful in at least 30 years. The phenomenon followed unprecedented rainfall that caused flash floods, damaging homes and forcing evacuations. The rain reached deep into the parched ground, awakening millions of dormant seeds, bulbs and tubers. Now, more than 200 species have burst into color, &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/08/nx-s1-6023812/chile-desert-el-nino" target="_blank"&gt;creating a breathtaking spectacle&lt;/a&gt; where every crevice is streaked with hues.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-152561" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 2706;         --source-height: 1522;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2706x1522+0+141/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fe1%2F3b%2Fc4576aa14f7f879c8f83e8b05046%2Fap26307590155292.jpg" class="img" alt="Comedian and actor Russell Brand leaves Southwark Crown Court in London, Tuesday, Nov. 3, 2026." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Comedian and actor Russell Brand leaves Southwark Crown Court in London, Tuesday, Nov. 3, 2026.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Alastair Grant/AP                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Comedian Russell Brand faces a "significant" prison sentence as a London court is &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/08/nx-s1-6033957/russell-brand-learn-sentence-found-guilty-rape-sexual-assault" target="_blank"&gt;set to announce his punishment&lt;/a&gt; today after a jury convicted him on three counts of sexual assault and one count of rape. Brand has denied all charges.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The U.S. homeless population &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/07/nx-s1-6033491/homelessness-in-the-u-s-saw-its-largest-drop-in-more-than-a-decade-last-year" target="_blank"&gt;decreased by more than 6%&lt;/a&gt; in 2025, according to the Department of Housing and Urban Development. This marks the second consecutive year of decline.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Pope Leo XIV arrived in South America on Friday for a 12-day trip across three countries. This will be his longest and &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/06/nx-s1-6026702/pope-leo-begins-12-day-3-country-tour-after-cancer-surgery" target="_blank"&gt;most significant journey to date&lt;/a&gt;, as well as his first major overseas visit since undergoing lung cancer surgery.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
