      <title>Democrats seize full control of Congress. And, which candidates made history last night</title>
      <author>Brittney Melton</author>
      <link>https://www.npr.org/2026/11/04/g-s1-151745/up-first-newsletter-midterms-democrats-congress-control</link>
      <comments>https://text.npr.org/2026/11/04/g-s1-151745/up-first-newsletter-midterms-democrats-congress-control</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.npr.org/2026/11/04/g-s1-151745/up-first-newsletter-midterms-democrats-congress-control</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 12:18:39 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;div id="storytext" class="storytext storylocation linkLocation"&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Good morning. You're reading the Up First newsletter. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/newsletter/news" target="_blank"&gt;Subscribe&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; here to get it delivered to your inbox, and &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/podcasts/510318/up-first/" target="_blank"&gt;listen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; to the Up First podcast for all the news you need to start your day.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Today's top stories&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Democrats have gained full control of Congress for the first time since 2023&lt;/strong&gt;, flipping &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/g-s1-149526/2026-midterms-congress-balance-of-power" target="_blank"&gt;both the House and Senate&lt;/a&gt; with significant wins in deep red states. &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/04/g-s1-150029/michigan-senate-race-abdul-el-sayed-mike-rogers" target="_blank"&gt;Abdul El-Sayed defeated&lt;/a&gt; Mike Rogers in Michigan, and &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/04/g-s1-148952/maine-senate-race-susan-collins-troy-jackson" target="_blank"&gt;Troy Jackson defeated&lt;/a&gt; Susan Collins in Maine, winning their states' closely watched Senate seats. In Texas, Democrat &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/g-s1-150844/gina-hinojosa-texas-governor-abbott" target="_blank"&gt;Gina Hinojosa defeated&lt;/a&gt; Republican Gov. Greg Abbott, ending more than 30 years of Republican control, while Democratic state &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/g-s1-148943/texas-senate-race-james-talarico" target="_blank"&gt;Rep. James Talarico won&lt;/a&gt; the U.S. Senate race. In Kansas, Adam Hamilton became the &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/g-s1-151587/kansas-senate-race-hamilton-marshall" target="_blank"&gt;first Democratic senator&lt;/a&gt; elected in nearly a century. A record number of candidates endorsed &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/03/g-s1-150034/2026-midterm-election-dsa-candidates" target="_blank"&gt;by the Democratic Socialists of America&lt;/a&gt; were elected to the House, growing the organization's presence on Capitol Hill. Nine states also made history with their &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/04/nx-s1-6028546/governor-candidates-history-election-2026" target="_blank"&gt;gubernatorial picks&lt;/a&gt;. Take a look at &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/04/nx-s1-6028080/voter-polls-midterms-demographics" target="_blank"&gt;how key demographics voted&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Here are &lt;a href="http://npr.org/nx-s1-6022216" target="_blank"&gt;6 midterm takeaways&lt;/a&gt; from NPR's senior political correspondent &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/392602474/domenico-montanaro" target="_blank"&gt;Domenico Montanaro&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-151679" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 5644;         --source-height: 3175;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5644x3175+0+290/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa8%2F74%2F5fb6a19f49719ca547f373fd6902%2Fap26154491239623.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5644x3175+0+290/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa8%2F74%2F5fb6a19f49719ca547f373fd6902%2Fap26154491239623.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5644x3175+0+290/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa8%2F74%2F5fb6a19f49719ca547f373fd6902%2Fap26154491239623.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5644x3175+0+290/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fn